MEDICAL NECESSITY CERTIFICATE

Date: 15th February 2026

To Whom It May Concern

Re: Patient Name: Mr. Arnav Saxena
     Age/Sex: 37 years/Male
     Hospital No.: HH-645702
     Diagnosis: Symptomatic Lipoma - Left Forearm

This is to certify that I have examined Mr. Arnav Saxena on 13/02/2026 in my outpatient clinic.

CLINICAL FINDINGS:

The patient presented with:
1. Swelling over left forearm - duration 1 month
2. Significant discomfort and pain at the site
3. Neurological symptoms - tingling and paresthesia in the left forearm
4. Restriction of normal movement

On examination, a well-defined subcutaneous mass measuring approximately 2.8 × 1 cm was palpable in the left forearm. USG imaging confirmed this as a lipoma in the subcutaneous plane of the left mid-forearm.

MEDICAL NECESSITY STATEMENT:

The surgical excision of this lipoma is MEDICALLY NECESSARY and NOT cosmetic for the following reasons:

1. The lipoma is causing documented pain and discomfort to the patient
2. There are active neurological symptoms (tingling/paresthesia) indicating possible nerve compression or irritation
3. The location and size of the lipoma warrant surgical removal to prevent further growth and worsening of symptoms
4. Conservative management has not provided relief

This is a THERAPEUTIC PROCEDURE aimed at:
- Relieving pain and discomfort
- Resolving neurological symptoms
- Preventing potential complications from an enlarging mass
- Restoring normal function and quality of life

This procedure is NOT being performed for aesthetic or cosmetic purposes. The primary indication is symptom relief and prevention of medical complications.

I recommend proceeding with surgical excision under local anaesthesia as a day care procedure at the earliest.


